From: PowerTune build fix <info@powertunedigital.com>
Subject: openat2 wrapper: add missing const to match current glibc prototype

pseudo's generated openat2() wrapper is declared without `const` on the
open_how* parameter. Current glibc declares the real openat2() with
`const struct open_how *`, and pseudo's own generated definition now
gets compiled in the same translation unit as glibc's declaration
(pseudo_wrappers.c includes <fcntl.h>), causing a hard conflicting-types
error:

  pseudo_wrapfuncs.c:11537:1: error: conflicting types for 'openat2';
  have 'int(int, const char *, struct open_how *, size_t)'
  note: previous declaration ... 'int(int, const char *,
  const struct open_how *, long unsigned int)'

Add the missing const so the generated wrapper's signature matches.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: PowerTune build fix <info@powertunedigital.com>

--- a/ports/linux/openat2/wrapfuncs.in
+++ b/ports/linux/openat2/wrapfuncs.in
@@ -1 +1 @@
-int openat2(int dirfd, const char *path, struct open_how *how, size_t size);
+int openat2(int dirfd, const char *path, const struct open_how *how, size_t size);
